      "discovery_teaching": {
        "prerequisite_note": "Identify a device and its local port before editing. This isolated example uses different devices from the assignment; LLDP transmit and receive settings act independently.",
        "concepts": [
          {
            "title": "Learn the directly attached port",
            "text": "LLDP advertises local chassis and port identity to the directly attached receiving port. A device does not forward its learned neighbor information to another port. This native simulator implements a bounded LLDP subset; CDP and IOS commands are not implemented."
          },
          {
            "title": "Transmit and receive are independent",
            "text": "An enabled transmitter can still advertise when its own receive setting is off. For both directions to learn, each transmitting endpoint must reach a live peer with reception enabled. Preserve unrelated ports, global settings and the physical link while repairing the requested receive setting."
          },
          {
            "title": "A cache records an advertisement",
            "text": "Applying settings does not automatically advertise. Send from each device explicitly. The receiver stores the advertised TTL; a newer advertisement refreshes it. Unexpired information can still be historical when advertised fields change. A current outcome also checks the current sender fields and ability to deliver."
          },
          {
            "title": "Time advances only when you request it",
            "text": "The simulated clock has no background scheduler. Advance time explicitly to age records; an entry expires exactly at its receive time plus its advertised TTL. Filling this example changes draft settings only and does not send advertisements or advance time."
          }
        ],
        "example_description": "In this separate practice topology, demo-oak can transmit but its uplink does not receive. Enable only that receive setting, apply the draft, then send an advertisement from demo-maple and from demo-oak. Inspect each current neighbor without changing the spare port or physical link.",
